That would be a nice idea. I have to admit that I got the idea from  
Hans Olberg, who wrote Lingua Latina (per se illustrata), which uses  
the natural method to teach Latin. I'm one of those horrid monolingual  
people for whom second language acquisition is very difficult. Lingua  
Latina is the only language learning resource which seemed to work for  
me.

Hans has his books on CD, along with recordings of him reading the  
chapters. So that's a really good idea, so as to improve listening as  
well as reading comprehension.

Let me incorporate all the feedback I've had so far, re-publish, and  
then we'll see what falls out.

